Z||000000||JamesWM83||08-14-2001||01:48 AM||||I've seen people turbo charging their 2.8's. I want to do this. Is there any turbos off of other cars that adapt to work this way? If so what cars do I get one from? thanks<P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000001||DreXteR||08-14-2001||05:04 PM||||Well youa can use almost any turbo form any car. For best match get one not too big but not too small. ehhehe Fun! T3 are a common pick, I doing it but in a dif way. I have a K26 and a K27, maybe will end in a hybrid - will be fun the last product. Also you will need some additional stuff for the project. Go to <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank> Dennis LaGrua</A> site for info. When my porject ends I will document all the info.<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/Fiero/Fiero1.jpg">  <BR>86 GT Turbo Intercooler Project - Total Restoration.||||reg||10
